                <pb facs="0342" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4597: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Magruder</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-19T13:00:00+01:00">July 19, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>24. Department’s telegram No. 14, July 3, 2 p.m. Yesterday, Portuguese Government
                    acceded to British invitation to adopt Hoover proposal but made reservations in
                    respect of reparations in kind and refrained from any public announcement.</p>
                <p>Under the circumstances does the Department still desire delivery of message?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Magruder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
